    <div class="alpheios-lex-entry" lemma-id="n35372" body-key=""><b><span class="alpheios-lex-la" lang="lat">per-plăcĕo</span></b> ,
			ēre, v. n., <div class="alpheios-lex-lex_sense alpheios-lex-lex_sense1"><b>I.</b><i>to please greatly</i>: 
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-la" lang="lat">ecquid placeant, me rogas? immo hercle vero
					perplacent,</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">Plaut.
					Most. 3, 3, 4</span></i>
			: 
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-la" lang="lat">servi mei perplacet mihi consilium,</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">id.
					Merc. 2, 3, 14</span></i>
			: 
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-la" lang="lat">perplacet (as affirm. answer),</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">Ter.
					Heaut. 5, 5, 22</span></i>
			 (Fleck. satis placet): 
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-la" lang="lat">ea (lex) mihi perplacet,</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">Cic.
					Att. 3, 23, 4</span></i>
			.</div>
